# LaTeX build intermediates.
#
# These are per-run state, not source. Committing them is what broke the build
# once already: a main.toc left over from a report-class ancestor of this
# document travelled with the repo, and pass 1 read its \contentsline{chapter}
# entries against an article-class main.tex, where \l@chapter does not exist.
#
# main.pdf and main.bbl stay tracked on purpose -- the PDF is the deliverable,
# and the .bbl lets `build.ps1 -Quick` produce a bibliography without bibtex.
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.blg
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# epstopdf output, regenerated from the .eps on every build
*-eps-converted-to.pdf
